<%- include('partials/legal-head') %>
      <p class="setup-eyebrow">Legal</p>
      <h1 class="setup-title">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="setup-lead">
        Influzer.ai is an MCP server directory, a WebMCP catalog, recipes, insights, a read-only Discovery MCP server, and a set of free creative tools. This policy explains what we collect when you use those services and how to reach us.
      </p>
      <p class="legal-meta">Effective 24 October 2026 · <a href="/support">Contact</a> · <a href="/cookie">Cookies</a> · <a href="/terms">Terms</a></p>

      <section class="legal-block">
        <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
        <p>
          Influzer (“we”) operates <a href="https://www.influzer.ai">https://www.influzer.ai</a>.
          Privacy questions go to <a href="mailto:hello@influzer.ai">hello@influzer.ai</a> or the <a href="/support">support page</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="legal-block">
        <h2>2. Information you give us</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Account.</strong> Email, name, and a password hash if you register with email. If you sign in with Google, or with Facebook when that option is shown, we store the provider id, email, name, and profile picture the provider sends.</li>
          <li><strong>Newsletter.</strong> Email address, the page you signed up from, and an unsubscribe token.</li>
          <li><strong>MCP listing.</strong> Your name, email, and the server details you submit. Submitting also adds that email to the newsletter unless you unsubscribe.</li>
          <li><strong>WebMCP scan.</strong> The URL you ask us to scan and the email you give for the report.</li>
          <li><strong>Comments.</strong> The display name and comment you post on an insight. Comments are reviewed before they appear.</li>
          <li><strong>Sponsored placement.</strong> Name, email, company, and listing URL. Checkout is handled by Stripe. We do not store your card number.</li>
          <li><strong>Email you send us.</strong> Whatever you include when you write to hello@influzer.ai.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="legal-block">
        <h2>3. Information collected automatically</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Page views.</strong> Path, IP address, country looked up from that IP, browser user agent, referrer, and your account id if you are signed in.</li>
          <li><strong>Discovery MCP</strong> (<code>https://www.influzer.ai/mcp/discovery</code>). We log the JSON-RPC method, tool name, whether the call succeeded, duration, IP address, user agent, and a client name such as Claude or Cursor. We do not store the search text you send to a tool.</li>
          <li><strong>Handshake probe.</strong> When a remote MCP URL is checked, we store the URL and the result (reachable, auth required, or unreachable, plus tool counts). We do not store credentials for that server.</li>
          <li><strong>Server logs.</strong> Request method, path, status, and duration.</li>
          <li><strong>Google Analytics</strong> on pages that load our analytics tag, including this one. The logo generator also loads Google AdSense.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="legal-block">
        <h2>4. Files from the free tools</h2>
        <p>
          Logos, favicons, converted video, and memes are stored on our servers so the download link works. We do not use those files to train models. They are not deleted on a fixed timer. Email <a href="mailto:hello@influzer.ai">hello@influzer.ai</a> if you want a specific file removed.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="legal-block">
        <h2>5. How we use this information</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Run the directory, Discovery MCP, accounts, newsletter, and free tools</li>
          <li>Review listings, comments, and sponsored placements</li>
          <li>Send the newsletter and service email you asked for</li>
          <li>Measure which pages and Discovery tools are used</li>
          <li>Limit abuse and keep the service available</li>
          <li>Meet legal duties</li>
        </ul>
        <p>We do not sell personal information.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="legal-block">
        <h2>6. Who else processes it</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Stripe</strong> — payment for a sponsored placement</li>
          <li><strong>Google</strong> — sign-in, Analytics, and AdSense on the logo generator</li>
          <li><strong>Facebook</strong> — sign-in, only if you use that option</li>
          <li><strong>Cloudflare Turnstile</strong> — spam check on insight comments</li>
          <li><strong>ip-api.com</strong> — country from the IP address on a page view</li>
          <li><strong>Our email provider</strong> — account mail and the newsletter</li>
        </ul>
        <p>We also disclose information if the law requires it, to protect the service, or as part of a merger or sale of the business.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="legal-block">
        <h2>7. Cookies and similar storage</h2>
        <p>
          A signed-in session uses the <code>connect.sid</code> cookie for 7 days. Theme and language preferences stay in your browser’s local storage, not in a cookie. Analytics and ad cookies are described in the <a href="/cookie">Cookie Policy</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="legal-block">
        <h2>8. How long we keep it</h2>
        <p>
          Account data stays while the account is open. Newsletter data stays until you unsubscribe. Page-view and Discovery logs stay so we can operate and secure the service. You can ask us to delete your account, newsletter address, comment, or a generated file.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="legal-block">
        <h2>9. Your rights</h2>
        <p>
          Depending on where you live, you can ask to access, correct, delete, or export your personal data, object to some processing, or withdraw consent. Email <a href="mailto:hello@influzer.ai?subject=Privacy%20request">hello@influzer.ai</a> with the address on the account or newsletter. You can unsubscribe from the newsletter with the link in any issue.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="legal-block">
        <h2>10. Children</h2>
        <p>Influzer is not for children under 16. We do not knowingly collect personal information from them.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="legal-block">
        <h2>11. Security and transfers</h2>
        <p>
          We use access controls and encrypted connections where the service is served over HTTPS. No method of transmission is perfectly secure. Data is processed on our hosting, which may be outside your country. We apply this policy to that processing.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="legal-block">
        <h2>12. Changes</h2>
        <p>We post updates on this page and change the effective date. Continued use of the site after the date means the updated policy applies.</p>
      </section>
<%- include('partials/legal-foot') %>
